//Compiler error messages
%PREFIX%=COMPILATIONERROR_

PROGRAM_MODULE_EXPECTED=Program expected but unit found
UNIT_MODULE_EXPECTED=Unit expected but program found
READ_PCU{0}_ERROR=Error at reading PCU file '{0}'
ASSEMBLY_{0}_NOT_FOUND=Assembly '{0}' not found
UNIT_{0}_NOT_FOUND=Unit '{0}' not found
SOURCE_FILE_{0}_NOT_FOUND=File '{0}' not found
NO_ACCESS_TO_FILE{0}=No access to the file '{0}'
CYCLIC_UNIT_REFERENCE_WITH_UNIT_{0}=Cyclic unit reference with unit '{0}'
UNDEFINED_SEMANTIC_ERROR{0}=Undefined semantic error : {0}
RESOURCEFILE_{0}_NOT_FOUND=Resource file '{0}' not found
DUPLICATE_USES_UNIT{0}=Duplicate identifier '{0}' in uses section
MAINRESOURCE_NOT_ALLOWED=mainresource can not be used with the directives: product, version, company, trademark, title, description, copyright
DUPLICATE_DIRECTIVE{0}=Duplicate directive {0}
FILE_{0}_NOT_FOUND=File '{0}' not found
NAMESPACE_CAN_BE_COMPILED_ONLY_IN_PROJECTS=Files with namespaces can be compiled only inside projects
NAMESPACE_CANNOT_HAVE_IN_SECTION=Namespace cannot have 'in' section
APPTYPE_DLL_IS_ALLOWED_ONLY_FOR_LIBRARIES=Parameter 'dll' in 'apptype' directive is allowed only for libraries
DISABLE_STANDARD_UNITS_DIRECTIVE_DISALLOWED_IN_USED_UNITS=Directive 'DisableStandardUnits' is disallowed in attached (by uses keyword) units 
USES_IN_WRONG_NAME=Unit name in uses-in ({0}) must be same as file name ({1})
UNSUPPORTED_TARGETFRAMEWORK_{0}=TargetFramework '{0}' is not supported
UNSUPPORTED_TARGET_PLATFORM{0}=Platform '{0}' is not supported
CONFLICTING_PACKAGE_VERSIONS{0}{1}{2}=Conflicting versions are specified for package '{0}': '{1}' and '{2}'
UNSUPPORTED_OUTPUT_FILE_TYPE{0}=Output file type '{0}' is not supported

PACKAGE_VERSION_ALREADY_REQUESTED{0}{1}{2}{3}{4}=Package '{0}' requires {1} in '{2}', but {3} was already requested in '{4}'.
PACKAGE_DEPENDENCY_REPLACEMENT{0}{1}{2}{3}{4}=Package '{0}' {1} was already selected by '{2}'. Packages from '{3}' would replace it with {4}. Already connected dependencies cannot be replaced.
PACKAGE_DEPENDENCY_REMOVAL{0}{1}{2}{3}=Package '{0}' {1} was already selected by '{2}'. Packages from '{3}' would remove it. Already connected dependencies cannot be removed.
PACKAGE_DEPENDENCY_RANGE_UNSATISFIED{0}{1}{2}{3}=Package '{0}' requires '{1}' {2}, but version {3} was selected.
PACKAGE_DEPENDENCY_RESOLVED{0}{1}{2}=NuGet: dependency '{0}' resolved to {1}; constraints: {2}.
PACKAGE_REQUIRES_RUNTIME_ASSEMBLY{0}=NuGet package '{0}' has only reference assemblies; the compiler needs a runtime assembly for semantic analysis.
PACKAGE_DUPLICATE_ASSEMBLY{0}=NuGet packages contain two different assemblies named '{0}'.
PACKAGE_RESTORE_FAILED{0}=NuGet package restore failed: {0}
PACKAGE_NOT_FOUND{0}=NuGet package was not found in the configured sources. Check the package ID and NuGet.Config. Details: {0}
PACKAGE_VERSION_UNAVAILABLE{0}=The requested NuGet package version is unavailable. Check the version or select an available one. Details: {0}
PACKAGE_SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE{0}=A NuGet package source is unavailable. Check your network connection and NuGet.Config. Details: {0}
REFERENCE_ASSEMBLY_CONFLICT{0}{1}=Assemblies '{0}' and '{1}' have the same internal simple name but different contents or identities. PascalABC.NET cannot reference both assemblies in one compilation.
ASSEMBLY_METADATA_READ_FAILED{0}=Cannot read assembly metadata from '{0}'.
REFERENCE_CONTEXT_NOT_UNLOADED=The previous reference AssemblyLoadContext is still referenced by the compiler.
REFERENCE_CONTEXT_CANNOT_RESOLVE{0}{1}=Reference context could not resolve '{0}'. Search directories: {1}.
UNSUPPORTED_DIAGNOSTIC_LANGUAGE{0}=Diagnostic language '{0}' is not supported.

%PREFIX%=
COMPILER_INTERNAL_ERROR_IN_UNIT_{0}_:{1}=Internal compiler error in module {0} :'{1}'
COMPILATIONERROR_WINDOWS_DESKTOP_REQUIRED{0}=Platform '{0}' requires Windows and the .NET 10 Windows Desktop Runtime.
